      "primaryConceptProposal": null,
      "secondaryConceptProposals": [],
      "taxonomyBlocker": "No approved mastery identity for readiness-level site selection is established. Site labels/objective topics and RTO context must not be silently promoted into canonical mastery roles.",
      "scenarioFamilyProposal": "budget-constrained-recovery-site-readiness",
      "familyRelation": "proposed_distinct_reasoning_pending_independent_gate",
      "familyRationale": "Choose an affordable recovery-site readiness level whose installed infrastructure and remaining software/data work can deliver the stipulated usable service. Unlike p211, the fastest hot-site option is infeasible on a hard budget while the tested warm package is sufficient; the cold package lacks installed resources. Unlike serial-recovery-dependency-budget, the main decision is selecting a preparation/cost package, not calculating whether one fixed runbook meets RTO. Shared timing and capacity reasoning is disclosed; editorial independence remains proposed, not psychometrically proven.",
      "familyIndependenceApproved": false,
